WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.560
Yakitate!! 9!
The fourth round.

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.150
Showdown in Oomagari.

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:09.320
The opponents are Suwabara and Monica,
who appeared disguised in ninja costumes.

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:13.080
I can’t hold it in anymore!

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:16.210
I’m going to take those masks of yours off!

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:17.960
Oomagari Shuriken,

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:19.830
Spring Onion Windmill!

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:25.620
Kawachi!
Kawachi-san!

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:31.990
Fire skill: Fried Spring Onion Technique!

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.560
Spring Onion Cloning Technique!

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:44.620
Come on, let’s go!

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:51.950
Yo! Ko! Sa! Wa!

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:57.380
This is really good spring onion.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:00.880
Being bent is...

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:04.000
Wo-n-der-ful!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.920
I got distracted by your technique and didn’t notice,

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.880
but now that I look, aren’t you Suwabara?!

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:12.760
Oh, no!

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:14.390
When I did the fire skill technique, I...

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:18.590
If I lose this battle, I will slash my stomach!

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:20.810
H-Hey, Kai...

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:23.360
When you say slash your stomach,
do you mean commit suicide?

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:24.440
Yes.

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:27.110
But, you just mean that you’re ready to do it.

00:01:27.110 --> 00:01:29.200
You’re not actually gonna do it, right?

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:30.270
I’ll do it.

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:32.400
I won’t let you die.

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:34.160
Monica...?

00:01:35.330 --> 00:01:36.490
Definitely...

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:38.040
We’ll definitely win!

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:38.660
Okay.

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:43.410
The local ingredients chosen by both parties

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:47.210
were bent spring onions,
chosen because they were bent.

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:52.670
Strangely, they both choose the same
ingredients, and the same method of preparation.

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:58.260
However, Suwabara had prepared
a secret technique to topple Azuma.

00:01:58.730 --> 00:01:59.730
Egg yolk?

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:02.310
Here, we have the former queen of the patisserie world.

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:04.020
We have you.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:06.150
We’ll have you make it.

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:09.150
With these famous Akita prefecture
Hinai chicken egg yolks,

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:11.480
we’ll have you make the ultimate blanchir.

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:14.030
I’ll steal the show from the something-or-other <i>Japan</i>.

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:16.320
Or rather, the Oomagari <i>Lupan</i>...

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:20.040
The Spring Onion Spiral <i>Lupan</i> will!

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:21.750
Just wait, Azuma,

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:26.540
and watch with your own eyes the hidden power
of a samurai who has laid his life on the line.

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:36.470
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:38.390
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:40.690
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:44.000
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:49.280
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:53.660
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:03.580
I want this voice to reach you, even though it’s still a tiny song.

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:09.750
That’s because I have the feeling that something’s gonna start.

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:24.850
As I was cowering, muffling my voice, the tears that I shed

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:33.440
probably helped me notice that

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:39.320
I’ve almost forgotten how to believe.

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:48.210
The future that I painted (I will fulfill it)

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:53.580
Looking up to the clear skies,

00:03:54.290 --> 00:04:00.720
I begin to run once again. Someday, I want to dye

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:06.510
that white sky with my colors.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:13.520
I’m going to fly as far as possible, shining like a marble,

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:17.900
unfolding these wings of mine.

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:26.710
I hate all things twisted!!

00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:29.510
Kai and Monica’s two-person tripod!

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:31.670
Azuma!

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:33.050
Hurry up, will ya?!

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:34.000
Azuma!

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:37.350
What’s wrong?

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:39.840
You still worried that we’re lacking in strategy?

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:41.770
It’s all right.

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:44.680
We’ll be able to make a really delicious spring onion bread with just that.

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:48.180
That’s true, but...

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:55.450
Kawachi-san, please close the front door, would you?

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:57.020
Oh, sorry about that.

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:58.620
All righty.

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:09.920
Whoa, that was a surprise.

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:12.120
It’s become quite spectacularly flat.

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:17.760
Since this lodge was a little too bent, I’d been kinda thinking that it was dangerous...

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:21.380
In that case, don’t settle on such a place,
no matter how cheap it is!

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:22.880
That’s it!

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:23.880
This is it!

00:05:24.230 --> 00:05:25.630
This...?

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:32.900
Azuma.

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:34.320
Just to be sure you know this...

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:35.560
My name is...

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:37.320
I know already.

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:39.700
Even without your telling me,
I’d have come at you with all I had.

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:40.940
Don’t worry.

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:44.910
Very well, then.

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:49.320
We will now begin the fourth round
of Yakitate!! 9 at Oomagari!

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:50.080
Start!

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:55.340
Manager...

00:05:55.340 --> 00:05:56.140
What is it?

00:05:56.590 --> 00:05:59.050
That ninja guy from the opponent’s side...

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:01.420
I get the feeling I’ve seen him somewhere...

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:03.650
You get the feeling, huh?

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:05.350
Kawachi-san!

00:06:05.350 --> 00:06:08.090
Not even one minute has passed since the start of the match!

00:06:09.230 --> 00:06:13.530
It’s all right for the commander to sit on his butt during the main show.

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:16.740
Does that pose have anything
to do with sitting on your butt?

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:18.740
What’s important are the preparations before the match.

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:21.560
It means that that’s where my power was put to full use.

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:22.910
Oh?

00:06:22.910 --> 00:06:25.190
So, what kind of power did you lend them?

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:30.460
Coming back to the subject of recognizing those ninjas...

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:31.920
Of course you would...

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:33.090
Ignoring me, huh?

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:35.950
After all, that ninja is Suwabara!

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:36.790
Huh?

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:37.670
Oh?

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:39.800
That is a surprise...

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:42.300
So, exactly what kind of power did you lend them?

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:44.180
I don’t know what the circumstances are,

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:46.680
but Suwabara joined up with St. Pierre.

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:48.640
At least that much is certain.

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:49.900
Kawachi!

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:51.700
Kawachi!

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:52.930
Kawachi!

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:55.440
But, don’t worry!

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:56.900
We’ll definitely win!

00:06:56.900 --> 00:06:58.070
So, be at ease.

00:06:58.070 --> 00:06:59.890
“We,” huh?

00:07:00.610 --> 00:07:01.940
I wonder about that...

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:06.490
He is, by nature, a guy who hates all things twisted.

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:11.240
He would have to really brace himself to be able to participate in something like this.

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:13.990
It’s possible for Azuma to lose this battle.

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:19.000
Wh-What’s with the uproar?

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:26.340
The ingredients are absolutely the same.

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:32.520
The methods of preparation are the same as well.

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:34.600
In that case, they’ll end up making the same bread!

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:35.940
It’s true!

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:38.780
Suwabara and Monica came up
with exactly the same idea!

00:07:38.780 --> 00:07:39.480
Didn’t I tell you that?

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:44.940
In this world, the strongest man is he who
has prepared himself to throw everything away.

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:48.790
Just as expected, Azuma.

00:07:48.790 --> 00:07:51.160
You came up with the same idea, huh?

00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:54.630
However, with just that, you
absolutely cannot win against me.

00:07:54.630 --> 00:07:55.920
Because...

00:07:55.920 --> 00:08:00.040
It looks like your blanchir is being whipped by Kanmuri.

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:04.640
But, he can’t compare in the preparation of cakes and sweets to the world’s #1, Monica.

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:07.880
Moreover... I have a secret weapon.

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:09.020
Monica!

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:10.310
Are you ready?

00:08:10.310 --> 00:08:11.560
I’m done.

00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:13.380
I mix it in with the dough there, right?

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:19.350
Now!

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:32.500
Th-That is...

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:33.240
Tourner?!
Note: Tourner means “to turn” in French.

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:35.080
Wh-What is that?
Note: Tourner means “to turn” in French.

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:35.920
Tourner.

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:38.170
It’s when you twist the
dough in one direction like that...

00:08:38.170 --> 00:08:39.290
A legendary technique.

00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:40.920
What’s that supposed to mean?

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:42.470
I’ve never even heard of it.

00:08:42.470 --> 00:08:43.630
Kawachi.

00:08:43.630 --> 00:08:45.470
When you twist dough,
what happens to it?

00:08:45.470 --> 00:08:47.290
Well...

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:52.190
Each twisted portion sticks to
the next twisted portion, so...

00:08:53.020 --> 00:08:54.550
Looks like you’ve realized it.

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:58.440
The portions that are twisted and stuck to each other are hard to warm.

00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:00.480
So, they keep fermenting
even during the baking process.

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:03.560
In other words, it expands more in the oven.

00:09:04.150 --> 00:09:07.570
When you add easily crushed ingredients raw into the dough,

00:09:07.570 --> 00:09:09.910
a process called unmixing occurs.

00:09:09.910 --> 00:09:11.570
This makes it hard for the bread to expand.

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:16.330
In order to overcome this, both
parties seem to have used blanchir.

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:20.790
But, Suwabara judged that to be
insufficient and has used a tourner.

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:25.790
Tourner is a technique said to have
been developed by French court chefs.

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:29.270
However, the slightest mistake would lead to the gas inside escaping,

00:09:29.270 --> 00:09:30.970
leaving it really disgusting.

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:34.800
That’s why these days, it isn’t
discussed outside of old cooking books.

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:37.650
And, that’s why it became a legendary technique, right?

00:09:37.650 --> 00:09:38.300
Yeah.

00:09:38.730 --> 00:09:40.440
Just as you’d expect of Suwabara...

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:43.320
It looks like he wasn’t just a plain old traitor.

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:45.360
This here is a tourner.

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:51.330
One of the <i>Lupan</i> series I created using stolen
techniques from various books and literary works.

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:54.970
Even if the ingredients and methods of preparation were the same until here,

00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:58.280
this match will be my victory.

00:09:58.790 --> 00:10:00.250
We did it, Kai!

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:02.920
It looks like you won’t have to slash your stomach after all.

00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:04.330
Yeah, so it seems.

00:10:05.090 --> 00:10:07.960
Now that I think of it,
it’s been a long journey...

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:15.010
Just eat my croissant without saying anything.

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:17.090
Will I be able to go to heaven?

00:10:17.810 --> 00:10:19.220
What?!

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:23.680
Dave-sensei and I went to heaven because of Azuma’s bread.

00:10:24.280 --> 00:10:26.690
As long as I can’t go to heaven with your bread...

00:10:26.690 --> 00:10:28.190
it’s your loss.

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:35.630
But, this time you are...

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:37.650
Wh-What?!

00:10:37.960 --> 00:10:39.910
Pantasia is doing something amazing, too!

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:46.050
The ninja twisted the dough,

00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:48.160
but this guy is folding it over.

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:49.560
I see...

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:52.050
It looks like at that time,

00:10:52.050 --> 00:10:54.870
Azuma-kun came up with this idea.

00:10:55.390 --> 00:10:56.920
Fondue, huh?

00:10:57.560 --> 00:10:59.020
What’s that?

00:10:59.020 --> 00:11:02.390
Like the tourner, it’s a technique
to help expansion within the oven.

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:06.780
The tourner uses the twisted
portions to help it expand in the oven.

00:11:06.780 --> 00:11:09.900
Similarly, the fondue expands in
the portions that are stuck together.

00:11:10.320 --> 00:11:13.370
I thought of using fondue in the beginning as well,

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:17.670
but I knew that the expansion of the tourner was just a little better in the oven, so...

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:19.910
I chose this one.

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:21.330
Is that so?

00:11:21.330 --> 00:11:23.290
But in that case, we’re all right.

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:24.160
Why do you say that?

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:27.380
Because, the tourner had the advantage, right?

00:11:27.380 --> 00:11:29.630
The breads have been made in the same way after all,

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:31.800
and the quality of our blanchir was better, too.

00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:34.850
In that case, it’s obvious that it’s our victory.

00:11:34.850 --> 00:11:36.300
Y-Yeah.

00:11:36.660 --> 00:11:38.390
Look here, Kai.

00:11:38.390 --> 00:11:41.800
Don’t you think that you’re
obsessing a little too much over Azuma?

00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:47.480
I know that he’s an amazing baker.

00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:52.270
But if you don’t concentrate on your own bread,
you’ll lose a battle that you’ve been winning.

00:11:52.270 --> 00:11:54.770
Th-That’s true.

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:58.290
Thank you for reminding me.

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:02.330
Monica, it’s as you say.

00:12:02.330 --> 00:12:05.280
During a match, I should concentrate on my own bread.

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:08.880
Let’s start the baking,
without worrying about the enemy!

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:09.750
Yep!

00:12:11.420 --> 00:12:12.750
All done.

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:15.010
This is my Oomagari <i>Lupan</i>!

00:12:15.010 --> 00:12:17.460
Also known as the Spring Onion Spiral <i>Lupan</i>!

00:12:18.810 --> 00:12:19.970
Come, Kuroyana...

00:12:19.970 --> 00:12:22.340
I mean, Mr. Judge.

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:23.820
You may eat.

00:12:28.610 --> 00:12:30.690
It looks like a delicious bread.

00:12:30.690 --> 00:12:35.600
But, for some reason... I feel like
I’ve eaten this ninja’s bread before.

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:37.160
What’s wrong?

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:38.670
Oh, sorry.

00:12:39.330 --> 00:12:40.500
Whatever.

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:42.490
Either way, I’ll know after eating.

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:08.770
Well, it looks like there wasn’t a big reaction.

00:13:08.770 --> 00:13:10.280
Yeah...

00:13:22.830 --> 00:13:25.420
He... He’s twisting!

00:13:25.420 --> 00:13:27.410
Kuro-yan’s twisted 360 degrees!

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:29.410
540 degrees?!

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:32.160
I don’t quite know, but he’s all twisted for sure!

00:13:33.210 --> 00:13:35.010
It was a wonderful bread.

00:13:35.010 --> 00:13:36.170
Mr. Mysterious Ninja.

00:13:36.170 --> 00:13:38.540
D-Don’t come near me, you monster!

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:40.100
Monster, you say?

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:43.550
How mean. If you say something like that...

00:13:44.180 --> 00:13:47.550
I’ll tell the whole country that you’re Suwabara.

00:13:47.900 --> 00:13:52.030
No matter who the baker is, their
bread is left with subtle peculiarities.

00:13:52.030 --> 00:13:54.870
I’m not so unskilled as to not be able to find that out.

00:13:57.660 --> 00:13:59.780
Then, do as you please.

00:13:59.780 --> 00:14:01.900
Either way, Azuma and the guys know about it already.

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:04.660
I will not run, nor will I hide.

00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:05.610
Shucks.

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:07.040
What the...

00:14:07.040 --> 00:14:09.000
The rest of them already knew?

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:10.120
How boring.

00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:11.750
Whatever.

00:14:11.750 --> 00:14:15.370
It’s certain that this bread was truly superb!

00:14:15.920 --> 00:14:19.220
I could feel your resolve through the bread.

00:14:19.220 --> 00:14:21.590
Whoa, it’s kinda awesome.

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:23.460
Just as you’d expect of Super Kuro.

00:14:24.430 --> 00:14:28.470
I’ve worked with you and with other artisans, after all.

00:14:30.020 --> 00:14:32.650
Then, this should be all right, I guess.

00:14:32.650 --> 00:14:34.350
Then, let’s eat it quickly.

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:36.480
This is my Oomagari <i>Japan</i>.

00:14:38.990 --> 00:14:40.490
D-Damn it!

00:14:40.490 --> 00:14:41.650
This shape is...

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:46.450
It looks like your face and hands are in opposite directions, so you can’t really pick it up, huh?

00:14:46.450 --> 00:14:48.410
In that case, I’ll feed it to you.

00:14:48.410 --> 00:14:49.150
Here you go.

00:14:56.010 --> 00:14:57.510
I have...

00:14:59.260 --> 00:15:01.040
lost this battle.

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:02.180
Wait!

00:15:02.180 --> 00:15:03.640
What happened, Kai?!

00:15:03.640 --> 00:15:05.520
We’ve almost won!

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:06.520
So, why?

00:15:06.520 --> 00:15:07.770
It’s impossible.

00:15:07.770 --> 00:15:09.890
Look carefully at Azuma’s bread.

00:15:09.890 --> 00:15:11.640
Th-This is...

00:15:12.110 --> 00:15:14.640
The folded portion was folded once again!

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:16.030
That’s right.

00:15:16.030 --> 00:15:19.780
In addition to using the fondue,
Azuma folded it once again.

00:15:19.780 --> 00:15:22.650
In other words, he did a double fondue.

00:15:23.240 --> 00:15:27.000
Both the amount of dough-to-dough contact and
the extent of expansion in the oven are doubled.

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:30.710
The difference between the expansion in the
oven of a regular tourner and fondue is slight.

00:15:30.710 --> 00:15:35.160
So, even with your blanchir to
make up for it, we cannot win.

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:37.920
We won’t know that unless we’ve tried it.

00:15:37.920 --> 00:15:40.430
Azuma might have made a mistake somewhere.

00:15:40.430 --> 00:15:43.170
Just looking at the bread, it’s clear
enough that there are no mistakes.

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:45.790
No, it’s just as this female ninja says.

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:48.890
For now, just let me eat that bread!

00:15:48.890 --> 00:15:49.980
If you do that...

00:15:49.980 --> 00:15:51.300
What are you, an idiot?!

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:53.810
If you eat this thing in the
shape that you’re in right now,

00:15:53.810 --> 00:15:56.650
all your bones will break, and you’ll die!

00:15:56.650 --> 00:15:58.690
Mind your own business!

00:15:58.690 --> 00:16:02.450
If I want to die eating bread,
then that’s my business!

00:16:04.490 --> 00:16:05.870
I can’t deal with you.

00:16:05.870 --> 00:16:07.080
Farewell.

00:16:07.620 --> 00:16:08.700
Wait, Kai!

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:10.880
Wait!

00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:15.410
Give my bread back to me, you asshole!

00:16:16.670 --> 00:16:17.590
That’s right.

00:16:17.590 --> 00:16:18.840
This is for the best.

00:16:18.840 --> 00:16:22.290
It’s best if only I, the traitor, die.

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:23.510
Don’t let him escape!

00:16:23.510 --> 00:16:24.790
Catch him!

00:16:30.680 --> 00:16:35.510
Since these people don’t do reactions,
it shouldn’t harm their lives.

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:36.520
I’m sorry, Azuma.

00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:37.980
I’m going to use this.

00:16:37.980 --> 00:16:40.330
Ninja skill: Double Fondue Technique!

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:46.950
Azuma’s bread has...

00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:51.330
You mean it is wonderful enough to
make complete amateurs have reactions?!

00:16:51.330 --> 00:16:54.070
If Kuroyanagi-san were to eat that bread...

00:16:54.290 --> 00:16:55.570
Farewell!

00:16:56.710 --> 00:16:57.800
Azuma...

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:03.290
I don’t really have the right to ask this of you, but...

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:05.170
What was that?!

00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:06.510
Slash his stomach?

00:17:06.510 --> 00:17:09.100
Suwabara is going to slash his stomach?!

00:17:09.430 --> 00:17:10.920
That’s what Kai said.

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:13.300
He just might do it, too...

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:15.810
Please... Save Kai!

00:17:15.810 --> 00:17:18.010
I don’t want Kai to die!

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:19.230
Of course!

00:17:19.230 --> 00:17:21.390
We won’t let that happen!

00:17:21.730 --> 00:17:23.530
But, what should we do...?

00:17:23.530 --> 00:17:25.530
Even if we were to go searching for Suwabara-san,

00:17:25.530 --> 00:17:27.770
without knowing where he went, it’s...

00:17:27.770 --> 00:17:29.330
That position...

00:17:29.330 --> 00:17:31.110
Let me take it.

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:34.160
B-But, Senpai!

00:17:34.160 --> 00:17:36.200
How do you plan on looking for him?!

00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:39.380
Don’t look down on me, a taste judge!

00:17:39.380 --> 00:17:44.710
It’s easy enough for my nose to pick up
on the scent of freshly baked bread.

00:17:45.800 --> 00:17:47.540
That sounds dependable!

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:50.510
Damn it. I don’t really care
if he kills himself.

00:17:50.510 --> 00:17:53.020
But I’m going to get that bread back at all costs.

00:17:53.020 --> 00:17:53.810
All right!

00:17:53.810 --> 00:17:55.100
It’s decided, then.

00:17:55.100 --> 00:17:56.050
Let’s hurry!

00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:58.070
All right!

00:17:58.440 --> 00:17:59.450
Sniff sniff.

00:18:00.360 --> 00:18:01.270
Sniff sniff.

00:18:01.650 --> 00:18:02.270
Sniff sniff.

00:18:02.920 --> 00:18:04.080
Sniff sniff.

00:18:06.650 --> 00:18:07.870
It’s close!

00:18:09.120 --> 00:18:10.030
There!

00:18:10.030 --> 00:18:12.110
In the middle of the river, right?

00:18:15.660 --> 00:18:18.370
The Omono River was once twisted.

00:18:18.370 --> 00:18:20.710
But now it has been made to flow straight.

00:18:20.710 --> 00:18:23.510
While it may have been for the sake
of the battle, I betrayed my friends.

00:18:23.510 --> 00:18:28.730
There is no place more suitable
for a man as twisted as I.

00:18:29.180 --> 00:18:31.600
Goodbye, everyone.

00:18:31.600 --> 00:18:34.560
I will die and become a straight man once again.

00:18:34.560 --> 00:18:36.340
Wait, Kai!

00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:39.090
Wait, Suwabara!

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:40.650
Monica!

00:18:41.310 --> 00:18:42.600
And, Azuma!

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:43.780
You idiot!

00:18:43.780 --> 00:18:45.100
What will you gain from dying?!

00:18:46.150 --> 00:18:47.310
You idiots are here, too?

00:18:48.610 --> 00:18:49.780
You there!

00:18:49.780 --> 00:18:51.860
You’ve been surrounded!

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:56.200
I don’t really care if you die,
but give me back the bread!

00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:57.080
Come on...

00:18:57.080 --> 00:18:58.460
This guy is...

00:18:58.460 --> 00:19:00.820
A true Bread Zombie...

00:19:01.380 --> 00:19:02.880
Either way...

00:19:02.880 --> 00:19:05.960
There’s no meaning to dying in this place all by yourself.

00:19:05.960 --> 00:19:08.040
No one wishes for that!

00:19:09.300 --> 00:19:12.220
Whether or not you wish it is not in question here.

00:19:12.220 --> 00:19:15.250
I want to die because I know I should to settle things.

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:16.720
Whatever.

00:19:16.720 --> 00:19:18.130
In that case, just die.

00:19:18.480 --> 00:19:19.300
Manager!

00:19:19.560 --> 00:19:21.810
But, just remember this!

00:19:21.810 --> 00:19:25.390
It’s because of that attitude that you lost to Azuma!

00:19:26.800 --> 00:19:28.390
Wh-What do you mean?!

00:19:28.390 --> 00:19:32.370
The reason Azuma never compromises
on his bread no matter what is because...

00:19:32.370 --> 00:19:34.410
he’s a responsible person!

00:19:34.410 --> 00:19:37.730
An irresponsible person like you cannot match him!

00:19:37.730 --> 00:19:39.330
What...?

00:19:39.330 --> 00:19:41.740
What part of me is it you find irresponsible?!

00:19:42.210 --> 00:19:44.170
You’re plenty irresponsible.

00:19:44.170 --> 00:19:47.790
As a man who’s dying,
leaving behind a pregnant woman.

00:19:48.130 --> 00:19:49.560
Right, Monica?

00:19:52.840 --> 00:19:54.750
What?!

00:19:57.720 --> 00:20:01.260
Is... Is that true, Monica?

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:04.260
Uh, ya... well...

00:20:09.110 --> 00:20:10.520
It’s true!

00:20:16.280 --> 00:20:18.200
How can this be...?

00:20:18.200 --> 00:20:20.960
My child in Monica...?

00:20:22.420 --> 00:20:23.790
Kai?

00:20:26.880 --> 00:20:28.120
Let’s go, Monica!

00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:29.620
Huh?

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:31.010
No huh’s...

00:20:31.010 --> 00:20:32.720
For now, let’s leave this place.

00:20:32.720 --> 00:20:33.790
Follow me!

00:20:34.340 --> 00:20:35.380
Okay!

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:36.930
Wait, you asshole!

00:20:36.930 --> 00:20:38.520
Leave the bread behind!

00:20:41.770 --> 00:20:44.350
Amazing how you come up with these lies...

00:20:44.350 --> 00:20:47.140
Can’t be sure if it’s a lie...

00:20:52.070 --> 00:20:54.100
We should be fine after coming this far.

00:20:55.160 --> 00:20:58.070
By the way, Monica...
Since when did you know?

00:20:58.950 --> 00:20:59.900
What?

00:21:00.620 --> 00:21:02.000
About the child!

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:04.400
Oh! Umm...

00:21:04.830 --> 00:21:07.450
For about a week...

00:21:07.840 --> 00:21:09.180
I see.

00:21:15.050 --> 00:21:16.850
Actually, Monica...

00:21:16.850 --> 00:21:22.810
One day, my father said that he was going to
master the way of the sword, and left home.

00:21:22.810 --> 00:21:25.470
We still don’t know where he is.

00:21:26.020 --> 00:21:31.950
Since childhood, I worked at a
neighborhood bakery to make ends meet.

00:21:32.490 --> 00:21:33.900
Is that so...?

00:21:34.860 --> 00:21:38.580
That is why, ever since then,
I’d decided deep in my heart...

00:21:38.580 --> 00:21:42.480
that a person who seeks to
master a path should not have children.

00:21:43.580 --> 00:21:44.620
But...

00:21:44.620 --> 00:21:47.090
Since you’re pregnant, it can’t be helped.

00:21:47.580 --> 00:21:51.680
I will train again, so that the
baby to be born will not be ashamed.

00:21:52.050 --> 00:21:54.580
And this time, I’ll be sure to win against Azuma.

00:21:55.630 --> 00:21:56.580
Kai...

00:21:56.580 --> 00:21:58.680
I’ll definitely win,

00:21:58.680 --> 00:22:01.710
to become a father that our child can be proud of.

00:22:02.220 --> 00:22:03.770
Monica.

00:22:03.770 --> 00:22:06.020
I’m not much of a guy, but...

00:22:06.020 --> 00:22:07.900
Kai!

00:22:08.770 --> 00:22:11.010
Kai! I love you!

00:22:13.150 --> 00:22:15.360
But, I’m really surprised.

00:22:15.360 --> 00:22:18.480
To think that we made a child between us...

00:22:19.070 --> 00:22:24.530
Do women really get pregnant
just by hugging a man like this?

00:22:26.660 --> 00:22:28.300
A mystery...

00:22:31.130 --> 00:22:32.800
All’s well that ends well!

00:22:32.800 --> 00:22:33.850
Right?

00:22:53.930 --> 00:23:02.230
The world will probably go on today, with a repetition of the same faces,

00:23:02.230 --> 00:23:10.280
but there was one thing that I’d forgotten.

00:23:10.700 --> 00:23:15.050
If I’m to take a deep breath,

00:23:15.050 --> 00:23:19.040
then the shape of the love that permeates my surroundings

00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:26.630
will shine so much that it’s blinding.

00:23:27.010 --> 00:23:35.010
Someone is calling me from far away...

00:23:35.390 --> 00:23:43.400
And that voice constantly echoes in my heart.

00:23:43.610 --> 00:23:51.990
So, riding on my small pleasures, the merry-go-round begins to turn...

00:23:51.990 --> 00:24:02.540
And even on days when the morning doesn’t come, it shines a light in my heart.

00:24:05.470 --> 00:24:06.390
Kanmuri-kun!

00:24:06.390 --> 00:24:09.170
I see some rather scary-looking brothers out here...

00:24:09.170 --> 00:24:10.520
Is that so...?

00:24:10.520 --> 00:24:12.980
I may no longer be able to continue as a baker.

00:24:12.980 --> 00:24:14.340
Goodbye, everyone!

00:24:14.340 --> 00:24:15.020
What was that?!

00:24:15.020 --> 00:24:16.270
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:16.270 --> 00:24:17.260
Kanmuri’s secret!!

00:24:17.260 --> 00:24:18.610
A jam showdown that lacks moral codes!

00:24:18.610 --> 00:24:19.970
Be sure to watch!

00:24:20.420 --> 00:24:22.730
Yakitate Seeds of Knowledge!!

00:24:23.100 --> 00:24:25.700
Among the ingredients in green onions is sulfur, which has a tranquilizing effect.

00:24:25.700 --> 00:24:27.100
If you cut some up and put them at your bedside,

00:24:27.100 --> 00:24:31.740
the relaxing scent of sulfur will allow you to sleep.

00:24:32.160 --> 00:24:34.730
Hueeeh??
